# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values.
# .env is gitignored and will never be committed — .env.example is the template that IS committed,
# so anyone setting up this project knows which variables they need.
#
# No secrets are needed yet — this site is fully static (no backend, no API calls).
# Add variables here the moment you introduce something that needs a key
# (e.g. a contact-form service, an analytics provider, a future API integration).
